wer/value "pre-multiplying by ${Φ}^{-1}$" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-336713/field-3/6ac468fbce4e2bfb1223edb3d46838300efcaa352410349e94ee2b80fa1fd925" :answer/id #uuid "9e3ac1ea-251b-5099-9cdb-3a635c1a3e68" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "adding $Φ$" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-336713/field-3" :answer-field/id #uuid "fc12adc1-7b82-552e-8249-73aad151c210" :answer-field/key "field-3" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/select :answer-field/correct "q-336713/field-3/08a383c0cd6483e92e91f2b1657bbc1cdf0d1ef2b71cc1c1a15f81f328755bb8" :answer-field/choices ["q-336713/field-3/d1aa86a131a1ca96e44bba21e54e2732575b1dbe4a9dbe6bd49933ee371c6148" "q-336713/field-3/08a383c0cd6483e92e91f2b1657bbc1cdf0d1ef2b71cc1c1a15f81f328755bb8" "q-336713/field-3/fb83a2a64257fd0db88480cbbfbfd15880d454885b303b14c12196ffa9d196ac" "q-336713/field-3/6ac468fbce4e2bfb1223edb3d46838300efcaa352410349e94ee2b80fa1fd925"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-336713/field-4/5c2b26694d51082d626c589650bab151801e4e5110b434138af23ca2a2e926ef" :answer/id #uuid "05c46f52-5573-587f-9a5a-72a3afe10515" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\text{L7}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-336713/field-4/f06a8441c4bec30e864c6c39be6abf4457946a31c6a745cafe755726146ff770" :answer/id #uuid "dfd1ea36-266d-5e9d-ab64-dd49a2b83f60" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\text{L5}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-336713/field-4/a5157e58f6b625734fa6f9911abf4ff73a0f21be4a77b07cc395bf09ed174d27" :answer/id #uuid "775251c8-f8da-55e1-a5ba-bd1095f7b547" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\text{L6}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-336713/field-4/4aba6ae530a1a9ae6a0e811a31dd556956a43739e9518d9a3cb43c8ffe3000ae" :answer/id #uuid "cd2e044b-4138-5c34-96c2-e25c6753638b" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\text{L2}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-336713/field-4" :answer-field/id #uuid "204b409a-e944-5726-8dca-243415133732" :answer-field/key "field-4" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/select :answer-field/correct "q-336713/field-4/5c2b26694d51082d626c589650bab151801e4e5110b434138af23ca2a2e926ef" :answer-field/choices ["q-336713/field-4/5c2b26694d51082d626c589650bab151801e4e5110b434138af23ca2a2e926ef" "q-336713/field-4/f06a8441c4bec30e864c6c39be6abf4457946a31c6a745cafe755726146ff770" "q-336713/field-4/a5157e58f6b625734fa6f9911abf4ff73a0f21be4a77b07cc395bf09ed174d27" "q-336713/field-4/4aba6ae530a1a9ae6a0e811a31dd556956a43739e9518d9a3cb43c8ffe3000ae"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-336713" :question/id #uuid "018e497f-687a-502a-9607-05584c937b92" :question/math-academy-id "q-336713" :question/problem "Consider the following system of differential equations:\n\n$$\n{x}^{′}(t)=Ax(t)+f(t)\n$$\n\nUsing the method of variation of parameters, we wish to find a particular solution in the form ${x}_{p}(t)=Φu(t),$ where $Φ$ is a fundamental matrix for the corresponding homogeneous system and $u(t)$ is a column vector of functions to be determined. A derivation of the formula for ${x}_{p}(t)$ is given below. \n\n$\\text{L1}:\\,$ ${x}_{p}(t)=Φu(t)$\n\n$\\text{L2}:\\,$ ${x}_{p}^{′}(t)=Φ{u}^{′}(t)+{Φ}^{′}u(t)$\n\n$\\text{L3}:\\,$ $Φ{u}^{′}(t)+{Φ}^{′}u(t)=AΦu(t)+f(t)$\n\n$\\text{L4}:\\,$ ${Φ}^{′}=AΦ$\n\n$\\text{L5}:\\,$ $Φ{u}^{′}(t)=f(t)$\n\n$\\text{L6}:\\,$ ${u}^{′}(t)={Φ}^{-1}(t)f(t)$\n\n$\\text{L7}:\\,$ $u(t)=\\int {Φ}^{-1}f(t)\\,\\text{d}t$\n\n$\\text{L8}:\\,$ ${x}_{p}(t)=Φ\\int {Φ}^{-1}f(t)\\,\\text{d}t$\n\nSelect the correct options in the following reasoning.\n\n$\\,$ Line $\\text{L4}$ follows from the fact that {{field-1}} matrix.\n\n$\\,$ Line $\\text{L5}$ follows from lines {{field-2}} by substitution.\n\n$\\,$ Line $\\text{L7}$ follows from line $\\text{L6}$ by {{field-3}} both sides of the equation.\n\n$\\,$ Line $\\text{L8}$ is obtained by substituting {{field-4}} into $\\text{L1}.$" :question/worked-solution "Let's examine each statement in turn.\n\n- We first consider line $\\text{L4}.$ Since $Φ$ is a fundamental matrix, its columns are solutions to the homogeneous system ${x}^{′}(t)=Ax(t),$ i.e., by substituting any column $c(t)$ of $Φ$ into the homogeneous system, we get\n\n$$\n{c}^{′}(t)=Ac(t),\n$$\n\nwhere ${c}^{′}(t)$ is the corresponding column of derivatives in $Φ.$ As a result, this means that ${Φ}^{′}=AΦ.$ Therefore, $\\text{L4}$ follows from the fact that $Φ\\text{ is a fundamental}$ matrix.\n\n- Next, we consider lines $\\text{L3}$, $\\text{L4},$ and $\\text{L5}.$ Let's substitute ${Φ}^{′}=AΦ$ from $\\text{L4}$ into $\\text{L3}:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}Φ{u}^{′}(t)+{Φ}^{′}u(t)=AΦu(t)+f(t) \\\\ Φ{u}^{′}(t)+\\cancel{AΦu(t)}=\\cancel{AΦu(t)}+f(t) \\\\ Φ{u}^{′}(t)=f(t)\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, $\\text{L5}$ follows from $\\text{L3}\\text{ and }\\text{L4}$ by substitution.\n\n- Next, we consider lines $\\text{L6}$ and $\\text{L7}.$ To get $\\text{L7},$ we are $\\text{integrating}$ both sides of the equation in $\\text{L6}:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\int {u}^{′}(t)\\,\\text{d}t & =\\int {Φ}^{-1}(t)f(t)\\,\\text{d}t \\\\ u(t) & =\\int {Φ}^{-1}f(t)\\,\\text{d}t\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n- Finally, we consider lines $\\text{L1},$ $\\text{L7},$ and $\\text{L8}.$ Substituting\n\n$$\nu(t)=\\int {Φ}^{-1}f(t)\\,\\text{d}t\n$$\n\nfrom $\\text{L7}$ into $\\text{L1},$ we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{x}_{p}(t) & =Φu(t) \\\\  & =Φ\\int {Φ}^{-1}f(t)\\,\\text{d}t.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, $\\text{L8}$ is obtained by substituting $\\text{L7}$ into $\\text{L1}.$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy :question/answer-fields ["q-336713/field-1" "q-336713/field-2" "q-336713/field-3" "q-336713/field-4"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "6c20cd9a-5734-5129-93db-55f6dc985b3a"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-336713"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id 17592186164724 :answer-field/correct 17592186164726 :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} [:db/retract 17592186167200 :question/answer-fields 17592186164719] {:db/id "q-336711/field-2/ma-v1/2b25b1caa37140e19b3ed84912ad55886555950efd002dc6ec11c27912e1f099/97b54c76802a0f72bdb4e6c4f25ce242d931106229b94218f1f3f1dd3d71c9cb" :answer/id #uuid "7fb02c88-36db-5d97-8f6d-fadde5f9b915" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "initial system of ODEs" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-336711/field-2/ma-v1/2b25b1caa37140e19b3ed84912ad55886555950efd002dc6ec11c27912e1f099/f151a88afc9174459a6d3004a10a844e948802482c4f1edfe7fb510398b8160c" :answer/id #uuid "4e916a55-2d55-5da0-9277-78517961b9e4" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "first shifting theorem" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-336711/field-2/ma-v1/2b25b1caa37140e19b3ed84912ad55886555950efd002dc6ec11c27912e1f099/78ce8b9f62690f0d663d565915a6113b3efa4bf92272f091ecfb7adf99c0e81e" :answer/id #uuid "565eb9ba-a54a-5524-a2ad-b5d0b99d7f77" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "line $\\text{L4}$" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-336711/field-2/ma-v1/2b25b1caa37140e19b3ed84912ad55886555950efd002dc6ec11c27912e1f099/ca492e308f46ba37f7133579720c1521cd3bcb8406f1dd89d81047dfb9fca809" :answer/id #uuid "31a14f31-5666-593f-a097-a499d23c3d47" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "solution of the system of ODEs" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-336711/field-2/ma-v1/2b25b1caa37140e19b3ed84912ad55886555950efd002dc6ec11c27912e1f099" :answer-field/id #uuid "1e11665d-81ce-5fef-a287-3cbfffa09549" :answer-field/key "field-2" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/select :answer-field/correct "q-336711/field-2/ma-v1/2b25b1caa37140e19b3ed84912ad55886555950efd002dc6ec11c27912e1f099/97b54c76802a0f72bdb4e6c4f25ce242d931106229b94218f1f3f1dd3d71c9cb" :answer-field/choices ["q-336711/field-2/ma-v1/2b25b1caa37140e19b3ed84912ad55886555950efd002dc6ec11c27912e1f099/97b54c76802a0f72bdb4e6c4f25ce242d931106229b94218f1f3f1dd3d71c9cb" "q-336711/field-2/ma-v1/2b25b1caa37140e19b3ed84912ad55886555950efd002dc6ec11c27912e1f099/f151a88afc9174459a6d3004a10a844e948802482c4f1edfe7fb510398b8160c" "q-336711/field-2/ma-v1/2b25b1caa37140e19b3ed84912ad55886555950efd002dc6ec11c27912e1f099/78ce8b9f62690f0d663d565915a6113b3efa4bf92272f091ecfb7adf99c0e81e" "q-336711/field-2/ma-v1/2b25b1caa37140e19b3ed84912ad55886555950efd002dc6ec11c27912e1f099/ca492e308f46ba37f7133579720c1521cd3bcb8406f1dd89d81047dfb9fca809"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id 17592186164709 :answer-field/correct 17592186164710 :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id 17592186164714 :answer-field/correct 17592186164716 :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id [:question/math-academy-id "q-336711"] :question/problem "Consider the following system of differential equations:\n\n$$\n{x}^{′}(t)=Ax(t)+f(t)\n$$\n\nUsing the method of variation of parameters, we wish to find a particular solution in the form ${x}_{p}(t)=Φu(t),$ where $Φ$ is a fundamental matrix for the corresponding homogeneous system and $u(t)$ is a column vector of functions to be determined. A derivation of the formula for ${x}_{p}(t)$ is given below. \n\n$\\text{L1}:\\,$ ${x}_{p}(t)=Φu(t)$\n\n$\\text{L2}:\\,$ ${x}_{p}^{′}(t)=Φ{u}^{′}(t)+{Φ}^{′}u(t)$\n\n$\\text{L3}:\\,$ $Φ{u}^{′}(t)+{Φ}^{′}u(t)=AΦu(t)+f(t)$\n\n$\\text{L4}:\\,$ ${Φ}^{′}=AΦ$\n\n$\\text{L5}:\\,$ $Φ{u}^{′}(t)=f(t)$\n\n$\\text{L6}:\\,$ ${u}^{′}(t)={Φ}^{-1}(t)f(t)$\n\n$\\text{L7}:\\,$ $u(t)=\\int {Φ}^{-1}f(t)\\,\\text{d}t$\n\n$\\text{L8}:\\,$ ${x}_{p}(t)=Φ\\int {Φ}^{-1}f(t)\\,\\text{d}t$\n\nSelect the correct options in the following reasoning.\n\n$\\,$ Line $\\text{L2}$ follows from line $\\text{L1}$ by {{field-1}} both sides of  the equation.\n\n$\\,$ Line $\\text{L3}$ is obtained by substituting $\\text{L1}$ and $\\text{L2}$ into the {{field-2}}.\n\n$\\,$ Line $\\text{L6}$ follows from line $\\text{L5}$ by {{field-3}} both sides of the equation.\n\n$\\,$ Line $\\text{L4}$ follows from the fact that {{field-4}} matrix." :question/worked-solution "Let's examine each statement in turn.\n\n- We first consider lines $\\text{L1}$ and $\\text{L2}.$ To get $\\text{L2},$ we are $\\text{differentiating}$ with respect to $t$ both sides of the equation in $\\text{L1}:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{x}_{p}^{′}(t) & =(Φu(t))^{′} \\\\ {x}_{p}^{′}(t) & =Φ{u}^{′}(t)+{Φ}^{′}u(t)\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n- Next, we consider lines $\\text{L1},$ $\\text{L2},$ and $\\text{L3}.$ Let's substitute ${x}_{p}(t)=Φu(t)$ from $\\text{L1}$ and ${x}_{p}^{′}(t)=Φ{u}^{′}(t)+{Φ}^{′}u(t)$ from $\\text{L2}$ into the initial system of ODEs:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{x}^{′}(t) & =Ax(t)+f(t) \\\\ Φ{u}^{′}(t)+{Φ}^{′}u(t) & =AΦu(t)+f(t)\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, $\\text{L3}$ is obtained by substituting $\\text{L1}$ and $\\text{L2}$ into $\\text{initial system of ODEs}.$\n\n- Next, we consider lines $\\text{L5}$ and $\\text{L6}.$ Since $Φ$ is a fundamental matrix, its columns are linearly independent. So, $Φ$ is invertible. Therefore, $\\text{L6}$ follows from $\\text{L5}$ by $\\text{pre-multiplying by }{Φ}^{-1}$ both sides of the equation:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{Φ}^{-1}\\cdot Φ{u}^{′}(t) & ={Φ}^{-1}\\cdot f(t) \\\\ ({Φ}^{-1}Φ)\\cdot {u}^{′}(t) & ={Φ}^{-1}\\cdot f(t) \\\\ {u}^{′}(t) & ={Φ}^{-1}\\cdot f(t)\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n- Finally, we consider line $\\text{L4}.$ Since $Φ$ is a fundamental matrix, its columns are solutions to the homogeneous system ${x}^{′}(t)=Ax(t),$ i.e., by substituting any column $c(t)$ of $Φ$ into the homogeneous system, we get\n\n$$\n{c}^{′}(t)=Ac(t),\n$$\n\nwhere ${c}^{′}(t)$ is the corresponding column of derivatives in $Φ.$ As a result, this means that ${Φ}^{′}=AΦ.$ Therefore, $\\text{L4}$ follows from the fact that $Φ\\text{ is a fundamental}$ matrix." :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy :question/answer-fields ["q-336711/field-2/ma-v1/2b25b1caa37140e19b3ed84912ad55886555950efd002dc6ec11c27912e1f099"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id "q-336715/field-1/78ce8b9f62690f0d663d565915a6113b3efa4bf92272f091ecfb7adf99c0e81e" :answer/id #uuid "7111386a-e5d8-5cdb-a66f-f02dbd4ed587" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "line $\\text{L4}$" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-336715/field-1/97b54c76802a0f72bdb4e6c4f25ce242d931106229b94218f1f3f1dd3d71c9cb" :answer/id #uuid "2a897221-37ea-5bb6-b275-4cfc67233526" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "initial system of ODEs" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-336715/field-1/f151a88afc9174459a6d3004a10a844e948802482c4f1edfe7fb510398b8160c" :answer/id #uuid "097d14c4-e611-5792-894f-b03f44e8142c" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "first shifting theorem" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-336715/field-1/ca492e308f46ba37f7133579720c1521cd3bcb8406f1dd89d81047dfb9fca809" :answer/id #uuid "fe3d5050-a532-515f-9518-7c2d0b76e796" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "solution of the system of ODEs" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-336715/field-1" :answer-field/id #uuid "786bc030-8484-5517-bec4-36f305101b6f" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/select :answer-field/correct "q-336715/field-1/97b54c76802a0f72bdb4e6c4f25ce242d931106229b94218f1f3f1dd3d71c9cb" :answer-field/choices ["q-336715/field-1/78ce8b9f62690f0d663d565915a6113b3efa4bf92272f091ecfb7adf99c0e81e" "q-336715/field-1/97b54c76802a0f72bdb4e6c4f25ce242d931106229b94218f1f3f1dd3d71c9cb" "q-336715/field-1/f151a88afc9174459a6d3004a10a844e948802482c4f1edfe7fb510398b8160c" "q-336715/field-1/ca492e308f46ba37f7133579720c1521cd3bcb8406f1dd89d81047dfb9fca809"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-336715/field-2/04d069a44bdfcbb7aeea2e3413cbeb8ec2d1c716ba6f3d2468c7908c9cee7685" :answer/id #uuid "8af13c11-5624-5e0c-9118-2d6f9ca35f22" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "adding $Φ$ to" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-336715/field-2/08a383c0cd6483e92e91f2b1657bbc1cdf0d1ef2b71cc1c1a15f81f328755bb8" :answer/id #uuid "48057f17-6d88-5f22-bcf4-10a4f70a368a" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "integrating" :db/ensure [:answer/v