ath :answer/value "\\text{L2}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-336716/field-3" :answer-field/id #uuid "e4c61339-d17f-5236-9070-4ff4df49e194" :answer-field/key "field-3" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/select :answer-field/correct "q-336716/field-3/5c2b26694d51082d626c589650bab151801e4e5110b434138af23ca2a2e926ef" :answer-field/choices ["q-336716/field-3/a5157e58f6b625734fa6f9911abf4ff73a0f21be4a77b07cc395bf09ed174d27" "q-336716/field-3/f06a8441c4bec30e864c6c39be6abf4457946a31c6a745cafe755726146ff770" "q-336716/field-3/5c2b26694d51082d626c589650bab151801e4e5110b434138af23ca2a2e926ef" "q-336716/field-3/4aba6ae530a1a9ae6a0e811a31dd556956a43739e9518d9a3cb43c8ffe3000ae"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-336716/field-4/f06a8441c4bec30e864c6c39be6abf4457946a31c6a745cafe755726146ff770" :answer/id #uuid "85b89e62-304e-5fed-9f97-0b7058582453" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\text{L5}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-336716/field-4/124b0c2eb11420d91f7684989e46375a3c1c904a04910b2d823439550b297bf2" :answer/id #uuid "7db248c4-3872-538e-b59e-d1314ab1d387" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\text{L4}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-336716/field-4/e04811e52d1b108844992320b02362618b439dac20ffc031cd3e9eda4c7aaa2b" :answer/id #uuid "9720eb8e-72ae-5e8f-965d-8334afa64ce0" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\text{L3}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-336716/field-4/042168976629a933b0d0ef460bdad0013cb33b8a34cdbca393ce80067da1046d" :answer/id #uuid "9b20c8f8-5d7c-5c97-b254-977b16d1f8af" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\text{L1}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-336716/field-4" :answer-field/id #uuid "732a9ca1-72ba-5a7d-acef-5a6ace7a24c9" :answer-field/key "field-4" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/select :answer-field/correct "q-336716/field-4/042168976629a933b0d0ef460bdad0013cb33b8a34cdbca393ce80067da1046d" :answer-field/choices ["q-336716/field-4/f06a8441c4bec30e864c6c39be6abf4457946a31c6a745cafe755726146ff770" "q-336716/field-4/124b0c2eb11420d91f7684989e46375a3c1c904a04910b2d823439550b297bf2" "q-336716/field-4/e04811e52d1b108844992320b02362618b439dac20ffc031cd3e9eda4c7aaa2b" "q-336716/field-4/042168976629a933b0d0ef460bdad0013cb33b8a34cdbca393ce80067da1046d"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-336716" :question/id #uuid "68ae00aa-e57d-5620-9c00-ead6febaac73" :question/math-academy-id "q-336716" :question/problem "Consider the following system of differential equations:\n\n$$\n{x}^{′}(t)=Ax(t)+f(t)\n$$\n\nUsing the method of variation of parameters, we wish to find a particular solution in the form ${x}_{p}(t)=Φu(t),$ where $Φ$ is a fundamental matrix for the corresponding homogeneous system and $u(t)$ is a column vector of functions to be determined. A derivation of the formula for ${x}_{p}(t)$ is given below. \n\n$\\text{L1}:\\,$ ${x}_{p}(t)=Φu(t)$\n\n$\\text{L2}:\\,$ ${x}_{p}^{′}(t)=Φ{u}^{′}(t)+{Φ}^{′}u(t)$\n\n$\\text{L3}:\\,$ $Φ{u}^{′}(t)+{Φ}^{′}u(t)=AΦu(t)+f(t)$\n\n$\\text{L4}:\\,$ ${Φ}^{′}=AΦ$\n\n$\\text{L5}:\\,$ $Φ{u}^{′}(t)=f(t)$\n\n$\\text{L6}:\\,$ ${u}^{′}(t)={Φ}^{-1}(t)f(t)$\n\n$\\text{L7}:\\,$ $u(t)=\\int {Φ}^{-1}f(t)\\,\\text{d}t$\n\n$\\text{L8}:\\,$ ${x}_{p}(t)=Φ\\int {Φ}^{-1}f(t)\\,\\text{d}t$\n\nSelect the correct options in the following reasoning.\n\n$\\,$ Line $\\text{L2}$ follows from line $\\text{L1}$ by {{field-1}} both sides of  the equation.\n\n$\\,$ Line $\\text{L7}$ follows from line $\\text{L6}$ by {{field-2}} both sides of the equation.\n\n$\\,$ Line $\\text{L8}$ is obtained by substituting {{field-3}} into {{field-4}}." :question/worked-solution "Let's examine each statement in turn.\n\n- We first consider lines $\\text{L1}$ and $\\text{L2}.$ To get $\\text{L2},$ we are $\\text{differentiating}$ with respect to $t$ both sides of the equation in $\\text{L1}:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{x}_{p}^{′}(t) & =(Φu(t))^{′} \\\\ {x}_{p}^{′}(t) & =Φ{u}^{′}(t)+{Φ}^{′}u(t)\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n- Next, we consider lines $\\text{L6}$ and $\\text{L7}.$ To get $\\text{L7},$ we are $\\text{integrating}$ both sides of the equation in $\\text{L6}:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\int {u}^{′}(t)\\,\\text{d}t & =\\int {Φ}^{-1}(t)f(t)\\,\\text{d}t \\\\ u(t) & =\\int {Φ}^{-1}f(t)\\,\\text{d}t\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n- Finally, we consider lines $\\text{L1},$ $\\text{L7},$ and $\\text{L8}.$ Substituting\n\n$$\nu(t)=\\int {Φ}^{-1}f(t)\\,\\text{d}t\n$$\n\nfrom $\\text{L7}$ into $\\text{L1},$ we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{x}_{p}(t) & =Φu(t) \\\\  & =Φ\\int {Φ}^{-1}f(t)\\,\\text{d}t.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, $\\text{L8}$ is obtained by substituting $\\text{L7}$ into $\\text{L1}.$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy :question/answer-fields ["q-336716/field-1" "q-336716/field-2" "q-336716/field-3" "q-336716/field-4"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "6c20cd9a-5734-5129-93db-55f6dc985b3a"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-336716"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id 17592186164093 :answer-field/correct 17592186164094 :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id 17592186164098 :answer-field/correct 17592186164102 :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id 17592186164088 :answer-field/correct 17592186164091 :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id [:question/math-academy-id "q-330877"] :question/problem "Consider the following system of differential equations:\n\n$$\n{x}^{′}(t)=Ax(t)+f(t)\n$$\n\nUsing the method of variation of parameters, we wish to find a particular solution in the form ${x}_{p}(t)=Φu(t),$ where $Φ$ is a fundamental matrix for the corresponding homogeneous system and $u(t)$ is a column vector of functions to be determined. A derivation of the formula for ${x}_{p}(t)$ is given below. \n\n$\\text{L1}:\\,$ ${x}_{p}(t)=Φu(t)$\n\n$\\text{L2}:\\,$ ${x}_{p}^{′}(t)=Φ{u}^{′}(t)+{Φ}^{′}u(t)$\n\n$\\text{L3}:\\,$ $Φ{u}^{′}(t)+{Φ}^{′}u(t)=AΦu(t)+f(t)$\n\n$\\text{L4}:\\,$ ${Φ}^{′}=AΦ$\n\n$\\text{L5}:\\,$ $Φ{u}^{′}(t)=f(t)$\n\n$\\text{L6}:\\,$ ${u}^{′}(t)={Φ}^{-1}(t)f(t)$\n\n$\\text{L7}:\\,$ $u(t)=\\int {Φ}^{-1}f(t)\\,\\text{d}t$\n\n$\\text{L8}:\\,$ ${x}_{p}(t)=Φ\\int {Φ}^{-1}f(t)\\,\\text{d}t$\n\nSelect the correct options in the following reasoning.\n\n$\\,$ Line $\\text{L4}$ follows from the fact that {{field-1}} matrix.\n\n$\\,$ Line $\\text{L6}$ follows from line $\\text{L5}$ by {{field-2}} both sides of the equation.\n\n$\\,$ Line $\\text{L7}$ follows from line $\\text{L6}$ by {{field-3}} both sides of the equation." :question/worked-solution "Let's examine each statement in turn.\n\n- We first consider line $\\text{L4}.$ Since $Φ$ is a fundamental matrix, its columns are solutions to the homogeneous system ${x}^{′}(t)=Ax(t),$ i.e., by substituting any column $c(t)$ of $Φ$ into the homogeneous system, we get\n\n$$\n{c}^{′}(t)=Ac(t),\n$$\n\nwhere ${c}^{′}(t)$ is the corresponding column of derivatives in $Φ.$ As a result, this means that ${Φ}^{′}=AΦ.$ Therefore, $\\text{L4}$ follows from the fact that $Φ\\text{ is a fundamental}$ matrix.\n\n- Next, we consider lines $\\text{L5}$ and $\\text{L6}.$ Since $Φ$ is a fundamental matrix, its columns are linearly independent. So, $Φ$ is invertible. Therefore, $\\text{L6}$ follows from $\\text{L5}$ by $\\text{multiplying by }{Φ}^{-1}$ both sides of the equation:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{Φ}^{-1}\\cdot Φ{u}^{′}(t) & ={Φ}^{-1}\\cdot f(t) \\\\ ({Φ}^{-1}Φ)\\cdot {u}^{′}(t) & ={Φ}^{-1}\\cdot f(t) \\\\ {u}^{′}(t) & ={Φ}^{-1}\\cdot f(t)\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n- Finally, we consider lines $\\text{L6}$ and $\\text{L7}.$ To get $\\text{L7},$ we are $\\text{integrating}$ both sides of the equation in $\\text{L6}:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\int {u}^{′}(t)\\,\\text{d}t & =\\int {Φ}^{-1}(t)f(t)\\,\\text{d}t \\\\ u(t) & =\\int {Φ}^{-1}f(t)\\,\\text{d}t\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id "q-337230/field-1/b02c2b1234b5d00aad657fb77e04dab7f3e0b85fe9ad336be51400bc87fda55d" :answer/id #uuid "a9705533-e0fc-5e2f-b307-0391172d952b" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "-8e^{-4t}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-337230/field-1" :answer-field/id #uuid "31dba337-28f6-5aca-9204-9834bcc8483b" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/blank :answer-field/correct "q-337230/field-1/b02c2b1234b5d00aad657fb77e04dab7f3e0b85fe9ad336be51400bc87fda55d" :answer-field/choices ["q-337230/field-1/b02c2b1234b5d00aad657fb77e04dab7f3e0b85fe9ad336be51400bc87fda55d"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-337230/field-2/954f2b2ecf089f1c43903a74f4575cff67408acc792f8a71c271fa3076456a3b" :answer/id #uuid "c510ed8d-43e1-5e59-afd5-2fc574b43aff" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "2" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-337230/field-2" :answer-field/id #uuid "b458c7db-a6f4-595f-a4e2-f4080afe8b12" :answer-field/key "field-2" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/blank :answer-field/correct "q-337230/field-2/954f2b2ecf089f1c43903a74f4575cff67408acc792f8a71c271fa3076456a3b" :answer-field/choices ["q-337230/field-2/954f2b2ecf089f1c43903a74f4575cff67408acc792f8a71c271fa3076456a3b"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-337230" :question/id #uuid "d4fc05ed-28f9-50f5-a2fb-760e91d4ee30" :question/math-academy-id "q-337230" :question/problem "$$\n{x}^{′}(t)=[\\begin{aligned}1 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 4\\end{aligned}]x(t)+\\overset{f(t)}{\\overset{⏞}{[\\begin{aligned}2 \\\\ -8\\end{aligned}]}},\\,Φ=[\\begin{aligned}{e}^{t} & 0 \\\\ 0 & {e}^{4t}\\end{aligned}]\n$$\n\nConsider the system of differential equations and the fundamental matrix of the corresponding homogeneous system above. Using the method of variation of parameters, compute ${Φ}^{-1}\\,f(t)$ and the particular solution ${x}_{p}(t)$ of the system.\n\n| ${Φ}^{-1}\\,f(t)=\\,\\,$ |  | $2{e}^{-t}$ |  | $\\,,\\,$ | ${x}_{p}(t)=\\,\\,$ |  | $-2$ |  |  |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- |\n|  | {{field-1}} |  |  | {{field-2}} |  |  |  |  |  |" :question/worked-solution "We'll look for a particular solution in the form\n\n$$\n{x}_{p}(t)=Φ\\,u(t)\n$$\n\nwhere $Φ$ is a fundamental matrix for the corresponding homogeneous system, $f(t)$ is the forcing column vector and\n\n$$\nu(t)=\\int {Φ}^{-1}\\,f(t)\\,\\text{d}t.\n$$\n\nIn our case,\n\n$$\nΦ=[\\begin{aligned}{e}^{t} & 0 \\\\ 0 & {e}^{4t}\\end{aligned}],\\,f(t)=[\\begin{aligned}2 \\\\ -8\\end{aligned}].\n$$\n\nSince $Φ$ is a fundamental matrix, it must be invertible. Using the formula for the inverse of a $2\\times 2$ matrix, we get the following:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{Φ}^{-1} & =\\frac{1}{{e}^{t}\\cdot {e}^{4t}-0\\cdot 0}[\\begin{aligned}{e}^{4t} & 0 \\\\ 0 & {e}^{t}\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & ={e}^{-5t}[\\begin{aligned}{e}^{4t} & 0 \\\\ 0 & {e}^{t}\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}{e}^{-t} & 0 \\\\ 0 & {e}^{-4t}\\end{aligned}]. \\\\ {Φ}^{-1}\\,f(t) & =[\\begin{aligned}{e}^{-t} & 0 \\\\ 0 & {e}^{-4t}\\end{aligned}][\\begin{aligned}2 \\\\ -8\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}2{e}^{-t} \\\\ -8{e}^{-4t}\\end{aligned}]\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, using our formula for $u(t),$ we obtain\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}u(t) & =\\int {Φ}^{-1}\\,f(t)\\,\\text{d}t \\\\  & =\\int [\\begin{aligned}2{e}^{-t} \\\\ -8{e}^{-4t}\\end{aligned}]\\,\\text{d}t \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}\\int 2{e}^{-t}\\,\\text{d}t \\\\ \\int -8{e}^{-4t}\\,\\text{d}t\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}-2{e}^{-t} \\\\ 2{e}^{-4t}\\end{aligned}].\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, our particular solution is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{x}_{p}(t) & =Φ\\,u(t) \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}{e}^{t} & 0 \\\\ 0 & {e}^{4t}\\end{aligned}][\\begin{aligned}-2{e}^{-t} \\\\ 2{e}^{-4t}\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}-2 \\\\ 2\\end{aligned}].\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy :question/answer-fields ["q-337230/field-1" "q-337230/field-2"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "7d23f2a1-55fa-5398-9016-dc6fbc55c97b"] :knowledge-point/questions [